# Literature Verification Log

## Topic: Agricultural Supply Chain Resilience in the Davao Region

### 1. AI Prompt Used

```text
Act as an Academic Research Associate specializing in Mindanao development studies.

Generate a literature review on agricultural supply chain resilience in the Davao Region from 2020–2025.

Requirements:
- Focus on banana, cacao, coconut, and coffee industries.
- Summarize findings from peer-reviewed journals, government publications, and policy reports.
- Discuss logistics, climate resilience, farmer cooperatives, market access, and post-harvest facilities.
- Use a formal academic tone.
- Do not invent statistics or citations.
- Clearly distinguish facts from recommendations.
- Present the output in Markdown.
```

---

## 2. AI-Generated Summary Audit

| AI-Generated Statement / Citation | Source Vetted Against | Status | Human Correction / Empirical Note |
|-----------------------------------|-----------------------|--------|-----------------------------------|
| "The Davao Region remains one of the country's leading producers of bananas and cacao." | Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) Agricultural Statistics | ✅ **Verified** | Confirmed through PSA agricultural production reports. |
| "Farmer cooperatives improve market access and strengthen bargaining power among smallholder farmers." | Cooperative Development Authority (CDA); Department of Agriculture (DA) | ✅ **Verified** | Government reports support the role of cooperatives in improving marketing efficiency. |
| "Poor road conditions and inadequate cold storage continue to affect agricultural logistics." | Department of Agriculture (DA) Regional Field Office XI Reports | ✅ **Verified** | Supported by regional infrastructure and logistics assessments. |
| "The Davao Region contributes over 70% of the world's cacao production." | Philippine Cacao Industry Roadmap; PSA | ❌ **Hallucination** | No official publication supports this claim. AI exaggerated the region's global contribution. |
| "Climate change increases transportation delays and post-harvest losses during heavy rainfall." | Mindanao Development Authority (MinDA); National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) | ✅ **Verified** | Climate adaptation reports identify weather disruptions as a major logistics challenge. |
| "Every municipality in Davao Region already has fully operational cold storage facilities." | Department of Agriculture Infrastructure Reports | ❌ **Hallucination** | Cold-chain facilities remain limited and unevenly distributed across municipalities. |

